WEBVTT

00:00:04.158 --> 00:00:06.741
[PHOENIX] December 31st:
Maya and I have been invited

00:00:06.825 --> 00:00:09.158
to ring in the New Year
with a luxurious trip on

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:12.075
the maiden voyage of a
one-of-a-kind railway liner.

00:00:12.158 --> 00:00:14.616
Now. The moment you've
been waiting for.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.200
We're proud to bring you the
ultimate in first-class travel.

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:20.116
Ladies and gentlemen.
The Silver Star Express!

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.200
This train is a
labor of love, folks.

00:00:22.283 --> 00:00:24.616
Love for the elegance of the
steam-powered locomotive,

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.033
and Japan itself.

00:00:26.116 --> 00:00:28.450
A gift to our society from
the Goldstruck Republic's

00:00:28.533 --> 00:00:30.908
prominent tycoon,
Avery Richman!

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.450
Mr. Richman sends his blessings.

00:00:34.533 --> 00:00:37.908
Sadly, he couldn't be here to
celebrate this occasion with us,

00:00:37.991 --> 00:00:41.575
but regardless, we'll be
departing soon, so all aboard!

00:00:41.658 --> 00:00:45.658
This is so cool!
A luxury choo-choo train!

00:00:45.741 --> 00:00:47.700
I think it's all very
nostal-chic.

00:00:47.783 --> 00:00:49.450
I think you mean nostal-gic.

00:00:53.116 --> 00:00:55.200
Ooh! Come on!

00:00:55.283 --> 00:00:56.741
Let's climb on board, Nick!

00:00:56.825 --> 00:00:58.158
[GUMSHOE]
Whoa, you two again?

00:00:58.241 --> 00:00:59.241
[gasps]

00:00:59.325 --> 00:01:00.741
[PHOENIX]
Hello, Detective Gumshoe.

00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:02.491
[MAYA]
Hello, judge. Judge?

00:01:02.575 --> 00:01:04.491
Hello. Nice day.

00:01:04.575 --> 00:01:07.075
We both sent in
a postcard and won a trip!

00:01:07.158 --> 00:01:08.866
I'm going on
an all-expenses paid tour

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.950
of the hot springs up north
on board this old-timey train!

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:14.700
Yeah? We got an invitation!

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.700
With a fancy wax seal!

00:01:16.783 --> 00:01:18.908
[CONDUCTOR]
All aboard!

00:01:18.991 --> 00:01:21.116
[train whistle sounds]

00:01:27.241 --> 00:01:28.783
[PHOENIX] What should have
been a fun journey aboard

00:01:28.866 --> 00:01:31.616
a luxury express train
turns into a debacle when

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.616
the Silver Star is taken over
by the fugitive Avery Richman.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:37.033
His demand?

00:01:37.116 --> 00:01:39.450
The retrial of a year-old case
in America that ended in

00:01:39.533 --> 00:01:42.575
a jury finding him
to be guilty of murder.

00:01:42.658 --> 00:01:44.408
Maya calls
Detective Gumshoe for help

00:01:44.491 --> 00:01:47.200
on her walkie talkie,
but it turns out the train car

00:01:47.283 --> 00:01:50.241
we're in seems to have
vanished without a trace.

00:01:50.325 --> 00:01:53.075
Wherever we are, the
Silver Star has been transformed

00:01:53.158 --> 00:01:54.700
into a courtroom on wheels

00:01:54.783 --> 00:01:57.783
as a truly unprecedented
trial begins.

00:03:36.700 --> 00:03:38.950
If you'd come to order,
court is now in session

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.950
for the trial of fugitive,
Avery Richman!

00:03:44.408 --> 00:03:45.950
Maya are you still holding up?

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:49.991
Yep. And I filled
in Gumshoe, too.

00:03:50.075 --> 00:03:52.033
We'll start with
Prosecutor Turnbull.

00:03:52.116 --> 00:03:54.158
Have you prepared
an opening statement?

00:03:57.033 --> 00:03:59.241
There's something each of
you needs to understand.

00:03:59.325 --> 00:04:01.491
The US court system
is completely flawless.

00:04:01.575 --> 00:04:04.200
This retrial is nothing
but a waste of our time.

00:04:04.283 --> 00:04:07.658
[RICHMAN growls]
If it were really infallible.

00:04:07.741 --> 00:04:10.116
I wouldn't have had to resort
to such drastic measures

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:11.825
to prove my innocence.

00:04:11.908 --> 00:04:14.366
Problem is... we're
completely in the dark.

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:16.866
I know basically nothing
about your conviction.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.783
Yes, that's true.
Please explain the case.

00:04:21.783 --> 00:04:24.283
I was not the prosecutor
at his first trial.

00:04:24.366 --> 00:04:25.450
But I am an official member

00:04:25.533 --> 00:04:27.575
of the United States
Attorney's Office.

00:04:27.658 --> 00:04:29.075
Which means I always
have a database

00:04:29.158 --> 00:04:31.741
of notable cases with me.

00:04:31.825 --> 00:04:33.825
I'll catch you up.

00:04:33.908 --> 00:04:35.325
One year ago,

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.741
at the All-American Trade
Federation's year-end ceremony,

00:04:38.825 --> 00:04:42.533
Secretary-General Benjamin
Cashanova was murdered.

00:04:42.616 --> 00:04:44.741
Mr. Cashanova saw
the Goldstruck Republic's

00:04:44.825 --> 00:04:47.158
financial might as a threat,
and was trying

00:04:47.241 --> 00:04:50.366
to boot it out of
America's economy.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:52.700
The accused, Avery Richman,

00:04:52.783 --> 00:04:54.241
wouldn't stand for this.

00:04:56.325 --> 00:04:59.158
[TRISTAN] Which resulted in the
incident during the ceremony.

00:05:01.991 --> 00:05:03.325
[TRISTAN]
This is a map of the venue

00:05:03.408 --> 00:05:05.325
where the crime took place.

00:05:05.408 --> 00:05:07.866
The red dot is where
the victim was shot.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.491
At the time, he was giving
a year-end speech.

00:05:11.575 --> 00:05:14.283
The yellow dot
is the origin of the shot.

00:05:15.658 --> 00:05:16.950
Upon hearing the gunshot,

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.741
everyone in attendance
looked in the direction

00:05:18.825 --> 00:05:20.491
that the sound came from.

00:05:20.575 --> 00:05:23.658
They found Avery Richman
standing in the corner.

00:05:23.741 --> 00:05:27.200
Officers already on the scene
restrained him immediately.

00:05:27.283 --> 00:05:29.033
When they searched Mr. Richman,

00:05:29.116 --> 00:05:32.325
they found a pistol within
his interior coat pocket.

00:05:32.408 --> 00:05:35.408
The barrel was still quite hot,
thus proving it was used.

00:05:35.491 --> 00:05:37.616
And Richman's were the
only prints on the gun.

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:40.241
I swear that I didn't
have a weapon on me that night.

00:05:40.325 --> 00:05:42.116
And yet, the police found one.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.991
It's obvious that you carried
the murder weapon.

00:05:45.075 --> 00:05:47.033
Not to mention,
you had a strong motive.

00:05:47.116 --> 00:05:48.116
[RICHMAN growls]

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:49.658
[PHOENIX grunts]

00:05:49.741 --> 00:05:51.116
[JUDGE] Everything does seem
to indicate that the defendant

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.366
is in fact the guilty party
in this homicide case.

00:05:54.450 --> 00:05:56.033
[TRISTAN]
Naturally.

00:05:56.116 --> 00:05:58.616
[PHOENIX] No wonder an American
jury questioned his innocence

00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.241
and put him away for life.

00:06:01.616 --> 00:06:04.658
What about the defense?
What do you make of this?

00:06:04.741 --> 00:06:06.241
Well, the pistol gives me pause,

00:06:06.325 --> 00:06:07.825
I have my doubts about it.

00:06:07.908 --> 00:06:09.200
Yeah, you heard the man.

00:06:09.283 --> 00:06:10.825
He says he wasn't
carrying a gun.

00:06:10.908 --> 00:06:12.533
That's right.
Not to mention,

00:06:12.616 --> 00:06:13.741
there was no way
to sneak a weapon

00:06:13.825 --> 00:06:15.075
into that venue.

00:06:15.158 --> 00:06:17.450
[TRISTAN] Except as the
ceremony's guest of honor.

00:06:17.533 --> 00:06:20.783
You would have been exempted
from security searches.

00:06:20.866 --> 00:06:22.241
And besides.

00:06:22.325 --> 00:06:23.825
There is no doubt that
the murder weapon

00:06:23.908 --> 00:06:25.866
belonged to the defendant.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.408
As you can plainly see,

00:06:27.491 --> 00:06:29.616
the pistol is registered
under his name.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.908
Yes, I do admit
that it was my gun.

00:06:31.991 --> 00:06:34.950
Although, someone could
have stolen and planted it.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.908
It was a plot to
frame me for murder!

00:06:36.991 --> 00:06:38.325
And do you have any proof?

00:06:38.408 --> 00:06:40.741
Well. No. Not yet.

00:06:40.825 --> 00:06:42.158
[TRISTAN]
Hmph.

00:06:42.241 --> 00:06:45.325
This prosecutor's sure not
doing us any favors here.

00:06:45.408 --> 00:06:47.116
It appears there's
no need to overturn

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.908
the original verdict after all.

00:06:48.991 --> 00:06:51.575
[PHOENIX] A-Ah! Your Honor!
Before you decide that,

00:06:51.658 --> 00:06:54.491
shouldn't we hear what the
witnesses have to say?

00:06:54.575 --> 00:06:56.616
I swear. You attorneys
never know when

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:58.200
to throw in the towel.

00:06:58.283 --> 00:07:00.658
[PHOENIX]
Aren't you an attorney yourself?

00:07:00.741 --> 00:07:02.700
[PHOENIX] Sir, you were in
attendance at the ceremony

00:07:02.783 --> 00:07:04.116
and witnessed the murder?

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:08.700
Yes. Edgar Piston of
the All-American CRY Foundation.

00:07:08.783 --> 00:07:11.075
I can't stress enough
how even the smallest detail

00:07:11.158 --> 00:07:13.116
could help, so was there
anything odd you noticed

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.325
about the incident?

00:07:14.408 --> 00:07:16.658
I mentioned
this a year ago, but...

00:07:16.741 --> 00:07:19.241
Mr. Cashanova did stop
in the middle of his speech

00:07:19.325 --> 00:07:20.783
right before he was shot.

00:07:20.866 --> 00:07:23.200
As though he was
taken aback by something.

00:07:23.283 --> 00:07:26.075
Oh, really? Any idea why?

00:07:26.158 --> 00:07:29.200
[CYLINDER] It must've
been the tray. I'm certain.

00:07:29.283 --> 00:07:30.575
[PHOENIX]
And you are?

00:07:30.658 --> 00:07:33.533
The name is Allan Cylinder,
member of the Council.

00:07:33.616 --> 00:07:35.741
What happened was, a waiter
dropped a tray on the floor

00:07:35.825 --> 00:07:39.158
making a clatter right in the
middle of the man's speech.

00:07:39.241 --> 00:07:40.700
Well, that's rude.

00:07:43.325 --> 00:07:45.616
[CYLINDER] The sound
distracted Mr. Cashanova,

00:07:45.700 --> 00:07:47.241
and the very next moment.

00:07:49.533 --> 00:07:50.700
Yes, that's right!

00:07:50.783 --> 00:07:52.241
I remember the waiter
dropping the tray right

00:07:52.325 --> 00:07:53.533
in front of me first.

00:07:53.616 --> 00:07:55.950
And then a gunshot
rang out after that.

00:07:56.033 --> 00:07:57.700
[PHOENIX] Where did you
hear the shot come from?

00:07:57.783 --> 00:07:59.241
While I know
it was close to me,

00:07:59.325 --> 00:08:01.158
I can't say where
with any certainty.

00:08:01.241 --> 00:08:03.283
Yes, and I was
standing nearby as well.

00:08:03.366 --> 00:08:05.033
Seriously, what kind
of waiter drops

00:08:05.116 --> 00:08:07.450
a tray in the middle
of an important speech?

00:08:07.533 --> 00:08:10.575
These five-star hotels
need better hiring managers.

00:08:10.658 --> 00:08:12.533
I don't think we should
be too hard on the help,

00:08:12.616 --> 00:08:14.991
considering the man
was injured and all.

00:08:15.075 --> 00:08:17.116
Injured? How so?

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.158
As I recall,
he had a bandage here,

00:08:19.241 --> 00:08:21.575
wrapped around his right hand.
So I assumed that he had--

00:08:21.658 --> 00:08:22.950
[TRISTAN]
That's enough.

00:08:23.033 --> 00:08:24.783
This has nothing
to do with the case.

00:08:24.866 --> 00:08:26.950
I fail to see how
eyewitness testimony

00:08:27.033 --> 00:08:29.533
is unimportant to
the trial at hand.

00:08:29.616 --> 00:08:31.158
[TRISTAN] Regardless,
Your Honor, you'll find this man

00:08:31.241 --> 00:08:33.450
guilty long before
the sun rises.

00:08:33.533 --> 00:08:34.450
[RICHMAN growls]

00:08:34.533 --> 00:08:35.658
Do something, Nick.

00:08:41.408 --> 00:08:43.283
[PHOENIX]
A question, Mr. Richman.

00:08:43.366 --> 00:08:44.783
Yes, sir?

00:08:44.866 --> 00:08:46.075
[PHOENIX]
Now you were the ceremony's

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:47.200
guest of honor, right?

00:08:47.283 --> 00:08:49.491
That's right. Yes, I was

00:08:49.575 --> 00:08:51.241
[PHOENIX] Then what were
you doing standing all the way

00:08:51.325 --> 00:08:52.700
over in the corner?

00:08:52.783 --> 00:08:54.116
Well, it's simply because--

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:55.950
The defense is clearly stalling.

00:08:56.033 --> 00:08:57.991
[JAM] I'm afraid I'm the
reason he was over there

00:08:58.075 --> 00:08:59.241
[GROUP gasps]

00:08:59.325 --> 00:09:01.158
[CYLINDER]
Madame Mytonbred?

00:09:01.241 --> 00:09:03.033
I remember it perfectly.

00:09:03.116 --> 00:09:06.158
The way Mr. Richman acted
like such a gentleman.

00:09:06.241 --> 00:09:08.700
Oh? What did he do specifically?

00:09:08.783 --> 00:09:10.450
Well, let me see.

00:09:10.533 --> 00:09:13.825
I was near the front of the
stage, listening to the speech.

00:09:13.908 --> 00:09:14.866
[JAM gasps]

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.408
How unfortunate!

00:09:16.491 --> 00:09:18.325
I'll bring you some
napkins at once.

00:09:18.408 --> 00:09:20.158
[BUTTER gasps]

00:09:20.241 --> 00:09:22.200
I walked to the table
at the end of the banquet hall

00:09:22.283 --> 00:09:24.158
because the napkins were there.

00:09:24.241 --> 00:09:26.950
Which explains why I was
in the corner of the room.

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:28.200
[PHOENIX]
Not long after,

00:09:28.283 --> 00:09:30.241
the trigger was pulled
on the fatal shot.

00:09:30.325 --> 00:09:32.533
[JAM] That's right. And
it was such a terrible fright

00:09:32.616 --> 00:09:34.283
that it caused me
to pass out.

00:09:34.366 --> 00:09:35.866
Dropping a tray is one thing,

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:38.450
but there's simply no excuse for
a waiter at a five-star hotel

00:09:38.533 --> 00:09:40.575
to spill champagne on a guest!

00:09:40.658 --> 00:09:43.783
Well, given the man's situation,
it was understandable.

00:09:43.866 --> 00:09:45.616
What was his situation?

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.366
I remember feeling
sorry for him

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:50.075
because he was waiting
on us with an injured hand.

00:09:50.158 --> 00:09:52.700
Injured how? Like it
was all bloody and stuff?

00:09:52.783 --> 00:09:56.075
I distinctly recall he was
wearing a bandage as he worked.

00:09:56.158 --> 00:09:58.700
It covered his right hand.

00:09:58.783 --> 00:10:01.241
You also saw a waiter
with a bandaged right hand?

00:10:01.325 --> 00:10:04.408
She's describing the
exact same thing I saw!

00:10:04.491 --> 00:10:06.950
I demand you cease this
pointless questioning at once!

00:10:07.033 --> 00:10:08.241
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:10:10.908 --> 00:10:13.075
The same bandaged right hand.

00:10:13.158 --> 00:10:14.991
Which means the two
witnesses must have seen

00:10:15.075 --> 00:10:17.116
the exact same waiter.

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:19.533
I would say that's
a natural assumption.

00:10:19.616 --> 00:10:20.741
Look at the timeline.

00:10:20.825 --> 00:10:22.950
His behavior's
highly suspicious!

00:10:23.033 --> 00:10:26.575
Immediately after he spilled
champagne on Mrs. Mytonbred,

00:10:26.658 --> 00:10:28.825
he ends up in the corner
of the room with Richman,

00:10:28.908 --> 00:10:32.366
who'd gone to retrieve napkins,
and drops the tray.

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:33.616
[gasps]

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:35.283
[PHOENIX] Almost like
this mysterious waiter

00:10:35.366 --> 00:10:37.658
followed him over to the table.

00:10:37.741 --> 00:10:39.116
[JUDGE]
He has a point.

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:40.866
After walking to the
other side of the room,

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.700
he dropped the tray, drawing
everyone's attention and then--

00:10:43.783 --> 00:10:46.616
Bang! A gun was discharged
from the same vicinity!

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:48.325
[RICHMAN gasps]

00:10:48.408 --> 00:10:50.908
And do we know
what this waiter was named?

00:10:52.825 --> 00:10:56.075
[TRISTAN] According to the
records, he's named Gale.

00:10:56.158 --> 00:10:57.575
All right!

00:10:57.658 --> 00:11:01.366
Does anyone here have any
idea where Mr. Gale might be?

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:03.908
Come to think of it,
I did notice there was a table

00:11:03.991 --> 00:11:05.575
left unoccupied during dinner.

00:11:05.658 --> 00:11:06.741
That's right.

00:11:06.825 --> 00:11:08.075
--Now that you mention it.
--[screaming]

00:11:08.158 --> 00:11:09.408
[GROUP gasping]

00:11:11.491 --> 00:11:14.033
Freeze! Everyone else wait here!

00:11:14.116 --> 00:11:15.200
[JUDGE gasps]

00:11:19.783 --> 00:11:20.825
[ATTENDANT B gasps]

00:11:20.908 --> 00:11:22.033
[PHOENIX]
What's going on?

00:11:22.116 --> 00:11:24.575
There's no question.
The Chrysanthemum Room.

00:11:27.325 --> 00:11:29.991
--Extinguisher!
--I got it!

00:11:30.075 --> 00:11:33.783
Oh, man. There's lots
of fires tonight.

00:11:33.866 --> 00:11:36.158
[PHOENIX gasps]
See that?

00:11:36.241 --> 00:11:37.950
[MAYA pants]

00:11:39.533 --> 00:11:41.658
What is going on back there?

00:11:41.741 --> 00:11:42.658
It's a fire!

00:11:42.741 --> 00:11:43.783
What?

00:11:46.033 --> 00:11:47.033
Hold on.

00:11:48.241 --> 00:11:49.408
--[TRISTAN] Give it here!
--[MAYA grunts]

00:11:58.075 --> 00:11:59.325
Oh. Was he stabbed?

00:11:59.408 --> 00:12:00.533
It looks like he's--

00:12:00.616 --> 00:12:05.075
[TRISTAN] Stay back!
There's no helping him.

00:12:07.491 --> 00:12:08.825
This is now a crime scene.

00:12:08.908 --> 00:12:10.158
Who was the victim?

00:12:10.241 --> 00:12:11.991
I'm positive the man was Gale.

00:12:12.075 --> 00:12:13.908
Somebody used a knife
to commit the murder.

00:12:13.991 --> 00:12:14.991
Impossible!

00:12:15.075 --> 00:12:16.783
Go back to the
dining car right away.

00:12:16.866 --> 00:12:19.033
I want you to inform everyone
onboard of what's going on

00:12:19.116 --> 00:12:20.700
and make sure none
of them try to leave!

00:12:20.783 --> 00:12:22.408
Right! Yes, sir!

00:12:22.491 --> 00:12:23.866
How could this have happened?

00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:26.033
He was such
an important witness.

00:12:26.116 --> 00:12:28.616
Maybe that's the exact
reason why he was murdered.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:31.200
Tell me! Do you know
who wanted him dead?

00:12:31.283 --> 00:12:33.283
I'm not sure. But, sir...

00:12:33.366 --> 00:12:35.783
I do know we have a killer
on this train with us!

00:12:35.866 --> 00:12:36.866
[gasps]

00:12:41.825 --> 00:12:42.991
[REGINA]
I'm so sorry.

00:12:43.075 --> 00:12:44.783
I really didn't mean
to shoot you.

00:12:44.866 --> 00:12:46.450
That's a relief,
but I need to find out

00:12:46.533 --> 00:12:47.908
where the dining car went.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:52.533
No. Couldn't be...

00:12:52.616 --> 00:12:53.950
Does this disappearing
trick mean that you

00:12:54.033 --> 00:12:56.283
--actually killed everybody?
--[REGINA gasps]

00:12:56.366 --> 00:12:57.450
If anything happens to them,

00:12:57.533 --> 00:12:59.741
I swear I'll make sure
they put you away.

00:12:59.825 --> 00:13:00.950
No. We would never.

00:13:01.033 --> 00:13:02.866
Our king made us
promise something.

00:13:02.950 --> 00:13:04.575
That no one would get hurt!

00:13:04.658 --> 00:13:06.700
Who's this "king"?

00:13:06.783 --> 00:13:07.908
King Richman!

00:13:07.991 --> 00:13:10.741
--Ouch! Arm!
--Oh, no. It was an accident!

00:13:10.825 --> 00:13:13.283
If you're truly
sorry. Then help me.

00:13:13.366 --> 00:13:15.741
We've got a mystery
to solve here.

00:13:15.825 --> 00:13:17.783
'Kay. But... How?

00:13:17.866 --> 00:13:20.033
What am I supposed to do?

00:13:20.116 --> 00:13:22.700
I need to have contact
with the outside world.

00:13:22.783 --> 00:13:25.700
No! The Japanese police
can't know what's going on.

00:13:25.783 --> 00:13:27.908
We have to obey
the king's orders!

00:13:27.991 --> 00:13:30.866
[GUMSHOE] Hmm.
Well, I suppose in that case.

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:33.200
I promise I won't
tip off anyone.

00:13:33.283 --> 00:13:35.116
Gumshoe's word.

00:13:35.200 --> 00:13:36.533
[REGINA]
Hmm.

00:13:36.616 --> 00:13:38.825
I'm not gonna double-cross you.

00:13:38.908 --> 00:13:40.241
Now, hurry!

00:13:43.116 --> 00:13:44.991
[REGINA] The king's trial is
currently being broadcast

00:13:45.075 --> 00:13:46.575
to a certain location.

00:13:46.658 --> 00:13:50.075
If you use that channel, you can
communicate with the outside.

00:13:50.158 --> 00:13:51.616
Pal. I owe you.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:54.325
Okay!

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:58.908
Please get this, I think
ya might be our only hope.

00:13:58.991 --> 00:14:00.075
Boom!

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:12.366
[phone vibrating]

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:13.950
[MILES]
Detective Gumshoe?

00:14:16.491 --> 00:14:17.700
What is this?

00:14:21.033 --> 00:14:22.825
[RICHMAN] I'd like you to
move out of the way, please.

00:14:22.908 --> 00:14:24.116
In a murder case,

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.950
preserving the crime scene
is extremely vital.

00:14:26.033 --> 00:14:29.158
I remember that
clumsy waiter's face very well.

00:14:29.241 --> 00:14:31.283
I must confirm
if it's actually him.

00:14:31.366 --> 00:14:33.075
You've forgotten your place.

00:14:33.158 --> 00:14:35.741
You're a murderer and
a fugitive of the law.

00:14:35.825 --> 00:14:37.783
Why would you get
to make demands here?

00:14:37.866 --> 00:14:38.950
And you seem to have forgotten

00:14:39.033 --> 00:14:41.325
who's running the
show here, prosecutor.

00:14:41.408 --> 00:14:43.866
I'm the one who holds all
the cards on this train.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:45.116
You got that?

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:54.408
No! The body...

00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.116
[PHOENIX]
It's gone?

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.075
What? But...

00:15:00.158 --> 00:15:01.658
That can't be possible.

00:15:03.908 --> 00:15:07.075
But we saw him.
With our own eyes.

00:15:07.158 --> 00:15:10.325
Where is the body?

00:15:13.116 --> 00:15:16.033
What the heck is going on?!

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:30.533
Huh? It looks like
this window doesn't open.

00:15:30.616 --> 00:15:32.491
[RICHMAN]
The door's the only way out.

00:15:32.575 --> 00:15:35.408
[PHOENIX] And we were
standing right in front of it.

00:15:35.491 --> 00:15:38.116
There's no way someone could've
gotten the body past us.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:40.991
A corpse does
not simply disappear.

00:15:41.075 --> 00:15:43.991
Oh! So this is like one of those
locked-room murder mysteries?

00:15:44.075 --> 00:15:47.950
Yeah. I don't know why you
sound so excited about that.

00:15:48.033 --> 00:15:50.408
--[TRISTAN] Look, an ID.
--[PHOENIX] Hmm?

00:15:50.491 --> 00:15:51.658
[RICHMAN]
There's no doubting it.

00:15:51.741 --> 00:15:53.575
He was the waiter.

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:57.491
[MAYA]
Hey. It's that guy!

00:15:57.575 --> 00:15:59.616
Where is the Chrysanthemum Room?

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:02.450
Yes. We did see him earlier,

00:16:02.533 --> 00:16:04.491
but only for a moment.

00:16:04.575 --> 00:16:06.075
Rick?

00:16:06.158 --> 00:16:08.200
I was wondering if there
was anything I could do

00:16:08.283 --> 00:16:09.366
to help you guys.

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:11.866
No. But I appreciate you asking.

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.658
As for the trial...

00:16:14.741 --> 00:16:16.366
It must be put off.

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:23.658
[MILES]
Avery Richman, huh?

00:16:23.741 --> 00:16:26.533
I can't be sure, but it looks
as though the prosecution

00:16:26.616 --> 00:16:30.450
was manipulating
evidence in this trial.

00:16:30.533 --> 00:16:32.658
Who was in
charge of planning it?

00:16:34.533 --> 00:16:37.033
[MILES]
The overseeing prosecutor was...

00:16:37.116 --> 00:16:39.325
...Tristan Turnbull.

00:16:39.408 --> 00:16:41.908
Turnbull? He did this?

00:16:41.991 --> 00:16:43.200
Cease and desist.

00:16:43.283 --> 00:16:44.366
You will accompany us

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.700
to the chief prosecutor's
office at once.

00:16:46.783 --> 00:16:48.825
I can't help but wonder
why it is you seem to have

00:16:48.908 --> 00:16:51.950
such a problem with me
inspecting Richman's case file.

00:16:52.033 --> 00:16:54.700
Why is it that some of
the testimonies were redacted?

00:16:54.783 --> 00:16:56.366
We have no answers for you.

00:16:56.450 --> 00:17:00.075
Now, quietly follow us this way.
Miles Edgeworth.

00:17:00.158 --> 00:17:01.491
Very well, then.

00:17:01.575 --> 00:17:04.241
I have several questions
for the chief, anyway.

00:17:06.741 --> 00:17:09.033
[PHOENIX] So, you said
this wasn't your case?

00:17:09.116 --> 00:17:10.991
I usually deal
with major international

00:17:11.075 --> 00:17:13.658
criminal cases, building
the prosecution's case

00:17:13.741 --> 00:17:15.366
for indictment and trial.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:18.283
Then it's out of my hands,
so I never stand in court.

00:17:18.366 --> 00:17:19.491
What was it that brought you

00:17:19.575 --> 00:17:21.658
out of the Attorney's
Office and overseas?

00:17:21.741 --> 00:17:23.741
[TRISTAN] I was on my first
vacation back to Japan

00:17:23.825 --> 00:17:25.200
in what felt like ages.

00:17:25.283 --> 00:17:27.075
That's when I
received this invite.

00:17:27.158 --> 00:17:29.075
I gotta say, I'm kinda
disappointed in the way

00:17:29.158 --> 00:17:30.908
you do things over there.

00:17:32.033 --> 00:17:33.116
Dial it back.

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:34.908
I mean, the American
court system totally

00:17:34.991 --> 00:17:36.450
overlooked Gale back then.

00:17:36.533 --> 00:17:38.366
[TRISTAN]
We didn't overlook him.

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.783
The truth is, we simply
concluded that he had

00:17:40.866 --> 00:17:42.700
nothing to do with the murder.

00:17:42.783 --> 00:17:44.866
I dunno. I bet Edgeworth
wouldn't have let that

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:49.158
whole bandage thing go if
he'd been the guy on the case.

00:17:49.241 --> 00:17:50.658
Edgeworth, you say?

00:17:50.741 --> 00:17:52.991
That's right. He's an
old friend of mine.

00:17:53.075 --> 00:17:56.283
He's a prosecutor,
so he's like Nick's rival.

00:17:56.366 --> 00:17:57.491
His rival.

00:17:58.908 --> 00:18:00.366
[TRISTAN] That argument
doesn't explain the numerous

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:03.033
contradictions to the witness's
testimony whatsoever.

00:18:03.116 --> 00:18:04.491
[ATTORNEY]
Well, but, you see...

00:18:04.575 --> 00:18:07.075
[TRISTAN] You must consider
any and all possibilities.

00:18:07.158 --> 00:18:09.450
You lack insight. Sorry, friend.

00:18:09.533 --> 00:18:11.533
[ATTORNEY groans]

00:18:11.616 --> 00:18:14.366
[TRISTAN] By the time I was
in my third year of law school,

00:18:14.450 --> 00:18:18.116
my name had become famous among
students and professors alike.

00:18:18.200 --> 00:18:20.200
They called me
the most brilliant pupil

00:18:20.283 --> 00:18:21.866
in the school's history.

00:18:23.033 --> 00:18:24.825
[MILES]
Objection!

00:18:24.908 --> 00:18:28.075
You're overlooking a very
real possibility yourself.

00:18:28.158 --> 00:18:29.825
What are you suggesting?

00:18:29.908 --> 00:18:31.616
Isn't it possible
that the witness is

00:18:31.700 --> 00:18:33.450
the one who is lying?

00:18:33.533 --> 00:18:35.575
[STUDENTS murmuring]

00:18:35.658 --> 00:18:38.200
How dare you
question me like this?!

00:18:38.283 --> 00:18:39.366
[MILES]
Among the testimonies,

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:42.116
this one sticks out
like a sore thumb.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:44.575
I believe it's a trap
set by the defense.

00:18:44.658 --> 00:18:46.075
[TRISTAN]
They're setting me up?

00:18:46.158 --> 00:18:49.408
But that would be against every
principle of a mock trial!

00:18:49.491 --> 00:18:50.908
A court debate must consider

00:18:50.991 --> 00:18:54.366
any and all possibilities.
That means there are no "rules."

00:18:54.450 --> 00:18:56.783
[TRISTAN gasps]

00:18:56.866 --> 00:18:59.533
It appears you lack
something, my friend--

00:18:59.616 --> 00:19:00.741
Insight.

00:19:00.825 --> 00:19:02.116
[TRISTAN] I felt I'd
caught a glimpse of what

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.325
real talent was like.

00:19:04.408 --> 00:19:06.408
After I graduated law school.

00:19:06.491 --> 00:19:09.200
I practically ran away
to America.

00:19:09.283 --> 00:19:11.866
And I've made it this far in my
career without finding myself

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:14.866
in his looming shadow.

00:19:14.950 --> 00:19:17.658
[PHOENIX]
Um... Mr. Turnbull?

00:19:17.741 --> 00:19:19.575
Forgive me.

00:19:21.491 --> 00:19:22.950
[CHIEF PROSECUTOR] I've been
told that you've requested

00:19:23.033 --> 00:19:25.658
the right to look over
the Richman case file.

00:19:25.741 --> 00:19:27.950
And why is that?

00:19:28.033 --> 00:19:29.866
Without getting into specifics.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:32.908
I find this trial to be
highly suspicious.

00:19:32.991 --> 00:19:34.283
[CHIEF PROSECUTOR]
Do you care to explain?

00:19:34.366 --> 00:19:36.366
[MILES]
Strange cross-examinations.

00:19:36.450 --> 00:19:38.116
Questionable evidence.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:41.241
It's hidden very well,
but I spotted the flaws.

00:19:41.325 --> 00:19:42.366
[CHIEF PROSECUTOR growls]

00:19:42.450 --> 00:19:44.491
I don't want to
believe it, but it bares

00:19:44.575 --> 00:19:48.825
every hallmark of
organizational malpractice, sir.

00:19:48.908 --> 00:19:50.033
How dare you!

00:19:50.116 --> 00:19:51.700
[ATTORNEY B]
America's justice system is--!

00:19:51.783 --> 00:19:52.950
[OLD ATTORNEY gasps]

00:19:53.033 --> 00:19:54.200
I'll be frank.

00:19:54.283 --> 00:19:56.450
Nobody in this room will
deny Avery Richman was

00:19:56.533 --> 00:19:59.575
a massive threat to the
United States' economy.

00:19:59.658 --> 00:20:01.283
However, that does not
mean we would ever

00:20:01.366 --> 00:20:03.200
manipulate our
courts in an effort

00:20:03.283 --> 00:20:04.575
to deal with the problem.

00:20:04.658 --> 00:20:05.783
Well then!

00:20:05.866 --> 00:20:08.033
What was the reason
you summoned me here?

00:20:08.116 --> 00:20:09.450
Let me be frank--

00:20:09.533 --> 00:20:11.616
If Richman was
declared guilty in a sham trial,

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:13.700
that verdict cannot stand.

00:20:15.991 --> 00:20:17.116
[CHIEF PROSECUTOR]
Apparently...

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.866
...you're not the only
one who thinks that.

00:20:23.241 --> 00:20:24.866
What's this?

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.241
Phoenix Wright?!

00:20:27.325 --> 00:20:28.825
[MILES] Detective Gumshoe
said something about

00:20:28.908 --> 00:20:32.158
a court on wheels.
Is this what he meant?

00:20:34.075 --> 00:20:35.575
[MILES]
Turnbull...

00:20:35.658 --> 00:20:37.825
[CHIEF PROSECUTOR] Richman's
taken control of the train

00:20:37.908 --> 00:20:41.241
and is holding
a retrial for himself.

00:20:41.325 --> 00:20:43.200
He claims that
he's going to shove

00:20:43.283 --> 00:20:45.491
the truth in our faces.

00:20:45.575 --> 00:20:47.116
Is that right?

00:20:51.866 --> 00:20:56.033
[GUMSHOE] Enter. C'mon!
Why isn't it working?

00:20:56.116 --> 00:20:57.533
Listen. It sounds
like the lightning

00:20:57.616 --> 00:20:59.491
is getting even closer.

00:20:59.575 --> 00:21:00.866
Would ya hurry up
and pass us along

00:21:00.950 --> 00:21:02.616
some info, Mr. Edgeworth?!

00:21:02.700 --> 00:21:03.950
[thunder cracks]

00:21:04.033 --> 00:21:05.366
[BOTH scream]

00:21:06.283 --> 00:21:07.408
--[thud]
--[BOTH gasp]

00:21:14.866 --> 00:21:15.991
[REGINA gasps, shrieks]

00:21:16.075 --> 00:21:18.408
He's dead.

00:21:18.491 --> 00:21:20.033
Huh.

00:21:21.700 --> 00:21:23.283
[GUMSHOE]
Must've fallen from there.

00:21:24.491 --> 00:21:25.991
I know this man.

00:21:26.075 --> 00:21:27.241
What's his name?

00:21:27.325 --> 00:21:30.575
Um... This is Mr. Gale.

00:21:30.658 --> 00:21:32.241
Is he a train attendant?

00:21:32.325 --> 00:21:35.366
He's not--Mr. Gale's a passenger
from Car Number 1.

00:21:35.450 --> 00:21:37.575
But the thing is,
he should be at the trial in

00:21:37.658 --> 00:21:39.616
the dining car right now!

00:21:39.700 --> 00:21:45.616
[GUMSHOE]
What's going on?

00:23:20.991 --> 00:23:22.283
[PHOENIX]
Objection!

00:23:22.366 --> 00:23:24.366
A murder, a missing body,
and the mystery

00:23:24.450 --> 00:23:26.283
of the vanishing train cars.

00:23:26.366 --> 00:23:29.991
As the abnormalities continue
mounting, the trial rumbles on.

00:23:30.075 --> 00:23:32.616
But then, Edgeworth
butts in from America!

00:23:32.700 --> 00:23:35.408
As the pieces fall into place,
the incident a year ago

00:23:35.491 --> 00:23:37.116
connects to the present.

00:23:37.200 --> 00:23:40.533
The Turnabout Express finally
rushes toward its conclusion!

00:23:40.616 --> 00:23:43.075
Find the contradictions!
Believe in the truth!

00:23:43.158 --> 00:23:46.741
Next episode: "Northward,
Turnabout Express--Last Trial"!

00:23:46.825 --> 00:23:48.075
Take that!
